# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini

# Secrets. The CourtListener token is read from the environment, never a file.
.env
*.token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately NOT committed, and why. The same reasoning appears in
# governance/freeze.toml's excluded block, because a reader arriving at either
# file asks the same question.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The DuckDB working database. Rebuildable from the committed csv artifacts in
# one command, large, and a binary that would churn on every run.
data/conformed/*.duckdb

# Fee-application PDFs retrieved from the RECAP archive. Potentially thousands
# of files and many gigabytes, and every one of them names individual
# timekeepers on nearly every page -- committing them would defeat the
# person-name control the rest of this repo implements. The freeze over this
# corpus is asserted by hash instead: data/raw/recap/manifest.csv is committed
# and src/validate.py recomputes every sha256 in it on every run. A fresh clone
# therefore has no corpus; re-fetch it with src/pull_fee_applications.py and
# check it against the manifest. That is a verified restore, not a re-pull.
data/raw/recap/**/*.pdf

# API response cache and the acquisition roster: working state of a resumable
# job, not evidence. The roster records which cases have been searched so a
# stopped run can continue; the cache exists so a resumed run does not re-ask
# questions it already has answers to.
data/live/
